o account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "  Intonation with Contrast", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Key words or words about new information in a sentence are stressed when you speak.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to emphasize one word or an idea over another, you change the sound of your voice. These are called <span class =\"strong\">contrast words</span>. You can show emotions or feelings by stressing contrast words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br />  Say these two sentences aloud. Stress the bolded words. How does the meaning change?<br /><br />  Sally studies <span class =\"strong\">Spanish</span>. <br/>Sally <span class =\"strong\">studies</span>  Spanish, but she doesn't <span class =\"strong\">use</span>  it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you stress the contrast words instead of key words, you can sound angry or frustrated.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br /> Say these three sentences. Stress the bolded words. Notice that the meaning of the sentence changes when you stress contrast words.<br /><br />   <span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>  said it is good.<br />  John <span class =\"strong\">doesn't</span>   like it.<br />   Where <span class =\"strong\">are</span>  they going tonight?<br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you stress modal verbs, it can have an opposite meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br />  Peter <span class =\"strong\">would</span>  help us, if he were here.<br />  People <span class =\"strong\">should</span>  exercise more, but many dislike it.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "church ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place of worship ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We went to church every Sunday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation at a restaurant.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "burger ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "short form of the word hamburger; a pattie inside a bun ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)  ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would like to order a burger and fries.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "purple ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the color of royalty ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I really like my purple purse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "surf and turf ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a mix of meat and seafood  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My surf and turf dinner had fish and beef.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mac and cheese ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a meal of noodles, cheese and a creamy sauce ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you finish all the mac and cheese?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "buckle ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something attached to the end of a belt to close it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like the buckle on your purse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": 